# Pairs with NoKeyLost. Applying the terminal clears the prepared bucket
# without draining it or applying the committed-values backstop, so an
# acknowledged batch is held nowhere.
MODULE: NoKeyLostTerminalDropsBucket
TARGET: NoKeyLost
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the terminal discards the bucket instead of draining it
PERTURBS: SagaTerminal

--- FIND
       IN /\ row' = [x \in Copies |-> [y \in Shards |-> [k \in Keys |->
                        IF <<x, y>> \in hit THEN TermRow(x, y, k) ELSE row[x][y][k]]]]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: nothing is drained into the projection.
       IN /\ row' = row
--- END